  "body": "## CamCraft 0.15.0\n\nA minor release headlined by multi-setup machining (setup tree #343, setup transform #316, carried stock #317, rest across setups #318, carried verify #319, stock source #320, fixtures/lathe/cache #321), inverted machine axes (#373, #374, #375), the Stock page / Theme ribbon button (#441), plus the other PRs merged since v0.14.0. Full notes in RELEASE_NOTES.md; 54 CHANGELOG rows; 59 decision files gathered into RECOMMENDED.md.\n\n### BREAKING\nProject files moved v50 -> v57. One WCS per setup, with G54-G59 only the post label (#342 / #354), and the setup defines the work offset instead of each height (#329 / #331). Files from 0.14.0 or earlier migrate on open; a project whose operations used different G54-G59 slots inside one setup is refused by name (open it in 0.14.0, align the slots, save). Older builds refuse files saved by 0.15.0.\n\n### Known issues\nOpen P0 #424 and #425 (fixture law: upright rapids check only the flute; ramps are judged at their lowest z), present before 0.15.0 and being worked.\n\n### Gate (scripts/release.ps1, release tier, no -SkipGate)\n- Debug: all non-UI crates plus camcraft-ui from crates/ui - 2820 passed, 0 failed, 67 ignored\n- Clippy over all crates, -D warnings - clean\n- Release --ignored lanes: motion 44 passed, sim 1 passed, app 17 passed, 0 failed\n- post.exe --version reports 0.15.0\n\n### Artifacts\ndist/camcraft-0.15.0-win-x64.zip built. No installer: ISCC.exe (Inno Setup) is not installed on this machine, so camcraft-0.15.0-win-x64-setup.exe was not produced.\n\nNot tagged, not merged: the tag follows the merge (AGENTS.md cut step 4).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n### Update after review\n- The full release tier above passed on 89a9f20. PR #446 (test-only, #445) merged to main afterwards and is merged into this branch; the delta was gated by `camcraft-motion --test swarf_pose_continuity` (5 passed, 0 failed, debug; not an --ignored lane) and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --tests -- -D warnings` (clean).\n- CHANGELOG: the docs-only README row (PR #301) is removed, PR-only rows now carry their issue numbers, and the one-file-per-operation row names PR #175. Release-mechanics PRs (e.g. #309 Arch/FreeBSD packaging) get no CHANGELOG row by rule; it stays in the user-visible RELEASE_NOTES.\n",
